<article class="env-definition" id="0FWX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FWX">Definition <span data-tag="0FWX">4.26.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a big<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000013317" id="a0000013317-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> category. An object $X$ of $\mathcal{C}$ is called a <em>categorically compact</em> if we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {C}(X, \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i M_ i) = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {C}(X, M_ i)  \]
</div>
  <p> for every filtered diagram $M : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{C}$ such that $\mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i M_ i$ exists. </p>
</article>